#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""miskatonic - a tile-based investigation game of the Cthulhu Mythos, in
Python + Tk.

Standard library only.  The engine is Penultimate's (one adventurer, a map
of squares, people to talk to by keyword, shops, dungeons), and the rules are
those of Call of Cthulhu, fifth edition: percentile skills, characteristics
rolled on 3D6, Sanity that drains away at the sight of things that should not
be, and investigators who are not fighting machines.

Arkham, Massachusetts, Thursday the 22nd of October, 1925.  Professor
Nathaniel Ashcroft of Miskatonic University has vanished, and with him the
four leaves of the Ashcroft manuscript: an incantation, the Rite of
Dismissal, that can close a door no one should open.  Dr. Henry Armitage,
the University's librarian, believes a cult, the Order of the Pale Lantern,
means to open that door on the stones of the river island at midnight on
Hallowe'en.  Find the four leaves, bring them to Armitage, and be on the
island before the stars are right.

Every new game makes a new case: the leaves lie in four of six places (a
mausoleum, the Witch House, the Sanitarium, the University's steam tunnels,
a Rivertown warehouse and a cave in the western woods), the people of Arkham
change, and one of its respectable citizens leads the cult.  Arkham itself
stays where it is.  The game is saved to ~/.miskatonic.json whenever you
change place and when you quit, and resumed next time.

Investigators: choose an occupation and roll characteristics (STR, CON, SIZ,
INT, POW, DEX, APP, EDU).  Occupation skill points (EDU x 20) and personal
interest points (INT x 10) are spent for you.  Hit points are (CON+SIZ)/2,
magic points POW, Sanity and Luck POW x 5.  Skills are rolled on D100: Spot
Hidden finds what's hidden (E searches), Listen hears what comes, Library
Use researches (walk into a library's shelves), Psychology sees through
liars, Persuade, Fast Talk and Credit Rating open doors, Locksmith opens
locks, Sneak keeps you unnoticed, Dodge keeps you whole.  Skills you use
well are checked, and improve when you bring a leaf to Armitage.

Sanity: the first sight of a horror costs Sanity (less if you make a Sanity
roll).  Lose 5 or more at once and an Idea roll that succeeds means
temporary insanity: fainting, panic, babbling or hallucinations.  Lose a
fifth of your Sanity within an hour and you gain a lasting disorder, until
the Arkham Sanitarium treats it.  Cthulhu Mythos knowledge, gained from
tomes and horrors, lowers your maximum Sanity (99 minus Cthulhu Mythos).
At zero Sanity, or dead, your investigator is lost; a friend takes up the
case, and the notes.

Talking: walk into a person (or into a counter with someone behind it),
then choose or type a word.  Everyone knows NAME, JOB and BYE; most people
know NEWS, and words in CAPITALS are worth asking about.  Shopkeepers
answer BUY.

Touch and mouse: tap a square to walk there, tap to aim, tap choices in
menus.  Gamepad (Linux, the Steam Deck): d-pad or stick moves, A waits or
chooses, B backs out, X fires, Y casts, LB uses an item, RB the journal,
View the map and Start the menu.

Sound effects and music are synthesized and played with afplay (macOS),
paplay or aplay if one is available, on Android with pyjnius, or with
pygame's mixer; otherwise the game is silent.  Music is cached in
~/.cache/miskatonic.

Keys: arrows or WASD move, Space waits, E searches, F fires and R reloads,
C casts, U uses or readies something, I shows your investigator, J the
journal, M the map, ? help.  The Rite of Dismissal must be spoken (C) in
the stone circle beneath the island, or at its threshold, and takes three
uninterrupted turns.

Arkham is the first place; the roads out of town (to Innsmouth, Kingsport,
Dunwich) and the bus and train clerks are where more places would go.

The tiles are drawn by the code below (PERSON_SHAPES, ART and
draw_terrain): no image files.  miskatonic --selftest builds every map,
room, level and tune of a few cases without opening a window.
"""

